A||N||2||Cozmo||Got thumped by a Toyota pickup yesterday...||||10||
Z||000000||Cozmo||11-29-2001||07:31 AM||||I was pulling away from a light yesterday(2,8 Muncie,'bout 2500 RPM 2nd. gear) when a Toyota pickup pulls up even on the right.  Then the guy kicks it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> big unmistakable SBC roar and tire squeal and he's 2 car lengths ahead and pulling away.  I finally got my wits together and floored it, by the time I got to 5000RPM he was still 2 car lengths ahead but NOT pulling away anymore <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>We shut it down and as I rolled up to him at the next light he was grinning like a Cheshire cat with the truck just sittin' there rumblin'...<BR>I gave him a thumbs up and say "That doesn't sound like any Toyota pickup I've ever heard... SBC, right?".<BR>He says "yup. 'vette motor. a real easy swap. I have a lot of fun with this thing.".<BR>He turns right, I go straight just shaking my head in awe...<BR>This truck looked stock but sure didn't sound or run that way.  He had a real problem with traction, tho... maybe didn't have enough ballast?<BR>I've been looking for a truck to haul Fiero stuff, maybe one of these is the ticket?<BR>(or a 350 S-10) <P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Cardone</B><BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thankssig.jpg">   <BR><B>'85 2M6 SE Targa</B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||mrfixit58||11-29-2001||08:14 AM||||My first custom motor vehicle was a 1972 Chevy L.U.V. truck. I removed the 4-banger and installed a SBC, TH350, and 8" Ford rearend. Even though te motor was only a 283, the power-to-weight ratio was enough to easily take most "factory" performance cars. The look on the faces of those guys driving the new 1983-84 Camaros, Firebirds and Mushtangs was priceless.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||14
